{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-unit-particle-state","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:unit-particle-state","kind":"definition","title":"The unit particle state $\\mathrm{Li}_q(z)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-local-cohomology-group"],"tags":["unit-particle","q-polylogarithm","generator","local-cohomology"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.UnitParticleState","text":"unit-particle-state.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/unit-particle-state.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:unit-particle-state\"></a><p>The <strong>unit particle state</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_q(z)</code> is the fundamental generator of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^1_{\\mathfrak{m}_1}(A)</code>. It uniquely satisfies the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-differential equation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  d_q \\mathrm{Li}_q(z) = \\frac{1}{\\log_q z} dz</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\log_q z = (z^{\\hbar_q} - 1)/\\hbar_q</code>. In the classical limit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1</code>, this recovers the classical dilogarithm <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_2(z)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/unit-particle-state.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"7.13.4"}
